    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change scenario analysis",
    "problem": "The prevailing scenario framework for climate change research lacks a systematic way to incorporate climate policy assumptions, hindering the consistent analysis and comparison of how different mitigation and adaptation strategies link socioeconomic pathways with specific climate outcomes.",
    "method": "This paper proposes the concept of Shared Climate Policy Assumptions (SPAs), which capture policy goals and instruments, as a third dimension to the scenario matrix to systematically link socioeconomic futures with climate outcomes and improve the comparability of climate change research.",
    "task": "The task is to present the concept of shared climate policy assumptions (SPAs) as a new dimension within the scenario framework to better link socioeconomic pathways with climate forcing outcomes for climate change research, impacts, adaptation, and mitigation.",
